{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>And in order that His fear be upon your faces.</b> Our Rabbis of blessed memory interpreted this as shame, for fear is an attribute of the heart, but since shame is visible and seen in the face, therefore it says 'upon your faces.' And He mentioned 'so that you do not sin,' to teach you that shame leads to fear of sin."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 20, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:01:36.666655687Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}